WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.300
Hi, this is geshe Michael Roach, 
welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:22.920
We've been talking about-- you know we're in the Steps of the Path for people of medium capacity and our goal is to get out of the Wheel of Life.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.900
In this level, the second level, 
the goal is to get out of the wheel of life,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.500
reach nirvana, a personal nirvana, just for ourselves,

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:38.280
and the method is to practice those three-- they're called the Three Extraordinary Trainings.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:50.260
These are being nice to other people, 
learning how to meditate or focus, 
and then mastering wisdom. Understanding emptiness.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.180
And if you remember, 
Pabongka Rinpoche said look,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:01.300
Getting perfect meditation and understanding emptiness, these are kind of big things

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.700
you have to have specialized help, 
you've got to work on them specially.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:13.320
But this one, being nice to other people, it's always right there in your hands. It's always available to you.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.480
You just have to do it. So no matter where you are,
no matter who you with you can practice this training.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.220
You don't need to have a meditation studio.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.820
You don't have to have the Perfection of Wisdom sutras.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.700
To be nice to other people you just have to be there.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:37.940
So we talked about three ways 
of not being nice to other people,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:44.180
or three things that might hurt your attempt 
to be nice to other people.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:51.460
So there are three different things that might happen to stop you from being nice to other people.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:02:02.680
The first one is that you don't know the guidelines 
for being nice. No one ever told you the 
guidelines for being a nice person.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:09.620
You can say the ten basic good deeds. These are nice guidelines. So at least you should know those ten.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:19.480
Or maybe you've gone deeper 
and taken lifetime layman's vows, or layperson's vows, which we should all do. At least that.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.700
And then if you want to go deeper and you want to get more committed than become a monk or a nun.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:32.100
So the first way to get in trouble 
is if you don't know what your vows are.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.240
No one ever told you what your vows are.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:44.700
And we said that particularly in the diamond way, particularly in the teachings which are meant to take you to enlightenment in one lifetime,

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.540
particularly those teachings depend on knowing the vows and keeping the vows.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:56.400
So if you ever take an initiation or an empowerment 
you should demand to be taught the vows.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:01.980
And that takes some time. That's going to take at least, 
I dont know, four or five days.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.880
Ideally it would take four or five weeks 
to teach you those vows correctly.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.340
Otherwise, you should not take an empowerment.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:19.540
So either you don't know the vows, 
or the second possibility for breaking them, 
is that they just don't sound very important to you.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.620
Like I understand I shouldn't kill people.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.060
And I understand I shouldn't steal things.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:33.560
But just talking about the president of the country 
when he is being weird?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.460
That's not on the same level 
as killing people or stealing things.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.470
That's not such a big deal.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.560
So this kind of attitude where you say @???

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.580
@? The idiom is @?
You say ah, that's not so important. I'm doing okay.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.620
I'm not going to kill anybody.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.820
I'm not going to steal anything.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:04:03.300
But having a glass of wine once in a while or sitting around and talking about politicians, that's okay. 
That's not such a big deal.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:14.300
So that kind of attitude where you decide unilaterally that the Buddha was being too strict.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:19.400
And the Buddha was micromanaging you.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:23.120
These morals are not very important.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:28.280
So that's the second possibility for breaking your vows.

